<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chahamanas of Ranastambhapura</h1><p class="st-meta">1192 CE – 1301 CE · capital Ranthambore</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Chauhan Rajput kingdom of Ranthambore fort, founded after Prithviraj III's defeat and famed for Hammira's defiance of Alauddin Khalji.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a> (Prithviraja III) of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chahamanas-of-shakambhari">Chahamanas of Shakambhari</a> fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> in 1192, his son Govindaraja was installed as a Ghurid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and moved to the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranthambore-fort">Ranthambore</a> (Ranastambhapura) in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>. His descendants ruled there as a separate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhan</a> line.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dynasty depended on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranthambore-fort">Ranthambore</a>, one of the strongest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a> of north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and alternated between submission to and revolt against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> captured the fort in 1226, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhans</a> regained it. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammira-deva">Hammira</a> expanded the kingdom by raids into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/udaipur-state">Mewar</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> inscriptions and the later epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammira-mahakavya">Hammira Mahakavya</a> record the dynasty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammira-deva">Hammira</a> sheltered Mongol rebels from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji's</a> army and refused to surrender them. After a long siege <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranthambore-fort">Ranthambore</a> fell in 1301 and Hammira was killed. The fall became a celebrated theme of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> heroic literature; the fort passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chahamanas-of-ranastambhapura.jpg" alt="Chahamanas of Ranastambhapura" width="320" height="228"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drachms_of_the_Chauhans_of_Ranthambhor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1192 CE – 1301 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ranthambore</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Govindaraja, Hammira</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Old Rajasthani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chauhans of Ranthambore, Kingdom of Ranthambore</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1246&amp;focus=chahamanas-of-ranastambhapura" aria-label="Chahamanas of Ranastambhapura on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6700 1222 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chahamanas of Ranastambhapura lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7020 1478L6969 1462M7020 1478L7018 1385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6969 1462h0M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7020 1478h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7020 1478h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1246&amp;focus=chahamanas-of-ranastambhapura">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
